      "description": "`ModalAction.shortcut` prop set by the confirm builder: `n` = cancel, `y` = proceed (so confirm dialogs get in-button accelerator letters for free once `button-shortcut-1` lands).\n\nFiles: confirm-dialog builder (`heca/src/chrome/...`), `ModalAction`/`ViewNode` prop wiring.\n\nBehaviors to preserve: confirm dialog semantics (Delete Pane? / Delete &lt;custom&gt?; verb \"Delete\"; disabled-OK-when-empty guard stays); the shortcut is additive metadata the Button reads to render its trailing accelerator slot. Update `docs/widgets.md`.",
